From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ksmbd: exempt FSCTL_PIPE_TRANSCEIVE from the generic file-id lookup

Backport of Gael Blivet's upstream fix, unchanged but for the hunk offset:
"[PATCH] ksmbd: exempt FSCTL_PIPE_TRANSCEIVE from the generic file-id lookup"
(linux-cifs, 2026-07-31), Reviewed-by and Tested-by ChenXiaoSong, applied by
Namjae Jeon to ksmbd-for-next-next (2026-08-03). Not in the pinned 7.2.8.

Upstream message:

  smb2_ioctl() rejects FSCTL_PIPE_TRANSCEIVE with STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND
  before fsctl_pipe_transceive() runs. RPC pipe IDs live in
  sess->rpc_handle_list, a separate namespace from the ksmbd_file table the
  generic ksmbd_lookup_fd_slow() gate searches, so the lookup always misses.

  Adding FSCTL_PIPE_TRANSCEIVE to the same no_fileid_ioctl exemption as
  FSCTL_PIPE_WAIT fixes it.

  Fixes: 0726814421c2 ("ksmbd: add SMB3 request replay support")

Why RetroForge carries it: the player's SMB shares (/etc/ksmbd/ksmbd.conf) could be
opened by URL but not listed. Measured on the MANGMI Pocket Max (2026-10-03):
`smbclient -L` failed with "rpc_pipe_bind for pipe srvsvc failed ...
NT_STATUS_CONNECTION_DISCONNECTED" for guests AND for an authenticated user,
with our [ipc$] and with ksmbd-tools' stock one; ksmbd debug showed "IPC pipe
create request" then "Failed to process 11 [-2]" (SMB2_IOCTL, -ENOENT), and
ksmbd.mountd never saw the RPC. So a file manager pointed at smb://retroforge.local/
showed nothing.

Origin: posted (applied to ksmbd-for-next-next). Drop when it reaches mainline
or the 7.2 stable series.

---
 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
--- a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
@@ -9634,6 +9634,7 @@ int smb2_ioctl(struct ksmbd_work *work)
 	case FSCTL_QUERY_NETWORK_INTERFACE_INFO:
 	case FSCTL_VALIDATE_NEGOTIATE_INFO:
 	case FSCTL_PIPE_WAIT:
+	case FSCTL_PIPE_TRANSCEIVE:
 		no_fileid_ioctl = true;
 		break;
 	default:
